ok 2 - Subset of a definite
# Subtest: Subset of a definite coercion
    1..3
    # Subtest: can't declare a variable without initializer
        1..2
        ok 1 - 'my OfDefCoerce $v' died
        ok 2 - right exception type (X::Syntax::Variable::MissingInitializer)
    ok 1 - can't declare a variable without initializer
    ok 2 - coerces correctly
    # Subtest: incorrect coercion into a typeobject throws on the subset
        1..2
        ok 1 - code dies
        ok 2 - right exception type (X::TypeCheck::Binding::Parameter)
    ok 3 - incorrect coercion into a typeobject throws on the subset
ok 3 - Subset of a definite coercion
# Subtest: Nested coercers
    1..5
    # Subtest: control: direct coercion fails as expected
        1..2
        ok 1 - code dies
        ok 2 - right exception type (X::AdHoc)
    ok 1 - control: direct coercion fails as expected
    # Subtest: assignment of unacceptable value to a variable fails
        1..2
        ok 1 - code dies
        ok 2 - right exception type (X::TypeCheck::Assignment)
    ok 2 - assignment of unacceptable value to a variable fails
    ok 3 - a chained coercion accepts an intermidiate target type
    ok 4 - nested coercions work for a scalar
    ok 5 - nested coercions work for function parameters
ok 4 - Nested coercers
